Subject: wayland backend: match presentation feedback events to their frame

The presented and discarded handlers took the oldest pending frame whatever feedback
object the event came for. Feedback events of different frames come in any order: a frame
replaced before it was shown gets discarded while the frame before it still waits for
presented (commit-timing makes that common). The wrong frame was then dropped, its feedback
object destroyed with its presented event, and every later presentation was attributed to
the frame before it for the rest of the session - a nested desktop at 240 Hz stayed at half
rate (2026-10-07, crosvm, after fast window operations under host GPU load). Match each
event to its frame by the feedback object; a presented frame drops the older ones still
waiting (they can no longer be shown).

From the research (virtio-gpu-desktop patches/kwin, 0028 FIX-H), ported to
6.7.5: its frames have no commitTime yet.

